# Krux release kernel: no crash-persisted data.
#
# An unlocked bootloader makes the runtime debug surface (dmesg,
# debugfs, kallsyms, SysRq, the serial console) a non-issue: anyone can
# boot their own kernel.  What matters is what this kernel leaves for
# the *next* kernel to read:
#
#   /proc/last_kmsg  <- CONFIG_ANDROID_RAM_CONSOLE
#   pstore/ramoops   <- CONFIG_RAMOOPS (and CONFIG_PSTORE)
#   core files       <- CONFIG_ELF_CORE (the stub also sets RLIMIT_CORE=0)
#
# ANDROID_PERSISTENT_RAM backs the ram console's reserved region; with
# both off there is no reserved log to hand to the next boot.
# CONFIG_PSTORE is already off in the defconfig, kept here for the
# record.
# CONFIG_ANDROID_RAM_CONSOLE is not set
# CONFIG_ANDROID_PERSISTENT_RAM is not set
# CONFIG_RAMOOPS is not set
# CONFIG_PSTORE is not set
# CONFIG_ELF_CORE is not set
